Viva Questions and Answers
Question	Answer
What is Salesforce?	Salesforce is a cloud-based CRM platform.
What is Apex?	Apex is the programming language of Salesforce.
What is Visualforce?	Visualforce is framework used to create GUI pages in Salesforce.
What is CRUD?	CRUD stands for Create, Read, Update and Delete.
What is a custom object?	Custom object is user-created database table in Salesforce.
What is a record?	Record is a row in an object.
What is controller?	Controller handles logic between GUI and database.
What is SOQL?	SOQL is Salesforce Object Query Language.
What is rerender?	It refreshes components dynamically.
What is pageBlock?	Visualforce component used for designing page sections.
Difference between Apex and Java?	Apex is cloud-based while Java is general-purpose.
What is commandButton?	Button used to execute Apex methods.
What is commandLink?	Link used to call controller methods.
What is Object Manager?	Tool used to manage objects and fields.
Why Salesforce is popular?	Because of cloud services and CRM features.
